<article class="page-wrapper">
  <div class="page-container page-container--wide">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="page-eyebrow">❓ KNOWLEDGE BASE & SUPPORT</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">Find immediate answers to common questions about the 2026 Sur-Ron Light Bee X, delivery, warranty, and technical setup.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="page-container">
      <!-- Group 1: Legality & Bike Specs -->
      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>🏍️ Vehicle & Legality</h2>
        <div class="faq-accordion">
          <details class="faq-detail" open>
            <summary class="faq-summary">Is the Sur-Ron Light Bee X street legal?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p><strong>No. The 2026 Sur-Ron Light Bee X is strictly an off-road electric dirt bike.</strong> It is not street legal for operation on public highways, streets, or sidewalks in most states and municipalities.</p>
              <p>It is engineered specifically for private land, closed racing circuits, and designated state or federal Off-Highway Vehicle (OHV) trail networks. Operating an off-road vehicle on public roads without state-approved conversion registration may violate traffic codes. Always consult your state's Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV) for local guidelines.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-detail">
            <summary class="faq-summary">What are the rider age and weight requirements?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We recommend riders be at least <strong>16 years of age or older</strong> with prior experience operating motorized two-wheel vehicles. Minors should always ride under direct adult supervision.</p>
              <p>The engineered maximum payload capacity is <strong>220 lbs (100 kg)</strong>. While riders exceeding this threshold may still operate the machine, acceleration dynamics, hill-climbing capability, suspension travel, and battery range will experience reduced performance.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-detail">
            <summary class="faq-summary">What is included in the crate when it arrives?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Every Bike Bee crate includes a complete, factory-fresh set of hardware:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>1x 2026 Sur-Ron Light Bee X Electric Dirt Bike (90% assembled)</li>
                <li>1x High-Output Fast Charger with USA 110V/120V wall plug</li>
                <li>1x 72V/35Ah or 60V/38Ah Removable Lithium-Ion Battery Pack with built-in BMS</li>
                <li>2x Ignition Keys & Battery Compartment Keys</li>
                <li>1x Heavy-Duty Front Wheel & Quick-Release Axle Assembly</li>
                <li>1x Front Fender Assembly & Hardware</li>
                <li>2x Ergonomic Gripped Footpegs & Mounting Hardware</li>
                <li>1x Comprehensive Metric Tool Kit for unboxing assembly</li>
                <li>1x Official Owner's Manual & Certificate of Quality</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-detail">
            <summary class="faq-summary">How much assembly is required upon delivery?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>The bike arrives <strong>approximately 90% pre-assembled</strong> inside an iron-reinforced protective freight crate. Final assembly typically takes <strong>30 to 45 minutes</strong> using the included metric tool kit.</p>
              <p>You only need to: (1) bolt on the handlebar and align the stem, (2) mount the front wheel and torque the front axle pinch bolts, (3) install the front fender, and (4) attach the left and right footpegs. All electronic wiring, throttle, controller, chain drive, and hydraulic brakes are factory-installed and pre-bled.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Group 2: Shipping & Delivery -->
      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>🚚 Shipping & Tracking</h2>
        <div class="faq-accordion">
          <details class="faq-detail">
            <summary class="faq-summary">How long does shipping take and how much does it cost?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We provide <strong>100% FREE Standard Freight Shipping on all electric dirt bikes to all 50 US States</strong> with zero shipping fees at checkout.</p>
              <p>Orders are processed, quality checked, and staged for carrier handoff in <strong>24 to 48 business hours</strong>. Freight transit time across the continental US is typically <strong>5 to 7 business days</strong>. Alaska and Hawaii generally require an additional 2 to 3 transit days.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-detail">
            <summary class="faq-summary">How do I track my order once it ships?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>The moment your freight carrier takes possession of your crate, our automated dispatch system sends you an email with your <strong>Carrier Tracking Number</strong> and direct tracking URL (FedEx Freight or UPS Freight).</p>
              <p>You can track the shipment's milestones 24/7. When the shipment arrives at your local destination terminal, the carrier dispatch desk will contact you via phone or SMS to schedule an appointment window for delivery.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-detail">
            <summary class="faq-summary">What should I do if my bike arrives damaged?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>All Bike Bee orders are <strong>100% insured against loss or damage in transit</strong> at no extra cost. If the crate appears visibly punctured, crushed, or damaged:</p>
              <ol>
                <li>Inspect the exterior before signing. <strong>Clearly write "DAMAGED UPON DELIVERY" on the carrier's Delivery Slip / Bill of Lading</strong> before the driver departs.</li>
                <li>Take multiple clear photos of the damaged packaging, shipping label, and damaged components.</li>
                <li><strong>Do NOT assemble or ride the bike.</strong></li>
                <li>Email <a href="mailto:contact@bikebee.shop">contact@bikebee.shop</a> within <strong>48 hours of delivery</strong>. We will immediately expedite replacement components or dispatch an entirely new bike under transit insurance.</li>
              </ol>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Group 3: Returns & Warranty -->
      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>🛡️ Returns, Warranty & Payments</h2>
        <div class="faq-accordion">
          <details class="faq-detail">
            <summary class="faq-summary">What is your 30-day return policy?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We offer a hassle-free <strong>30-Day Money-Back Guarantee</strong> commencing from the date of carrier delivery. To be eligible for a refund, the machine must be in <strong>100% brand-new, unridden, and unused condition</strong> in its original crate packaging with all included tools, keys, charger, and manuals intact.</p>
              <p>If you wish to initiate a return, email <a href="mailto:contact@bikebee.shop">contact@bikebee.shop</a> to receive an official Return Authorization (RA) number and return freight instructions. See our <a href="/pages/refund-policy">Refund & Return Policy</a> for full details.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-detail">
            <summary class="faq-summary">What does the 100-day warranty cover?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>All new Bike Bee bikes come standard with our <strong>100-Day Limited Manufacturer Warranty</strong> covering:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Permanent magnet synchronous electric motor internal failure.</li>
                <li>Lithium-ion power battery pack and integrated Battery Management System (BMS).</li>
                <li>Sine-wave electronic motor controller and digital throttle.</li>
                <li>Aluminum alloy frame structural welds and manufacturing defects.</li>
              </ul>
              <p>The warranty does not cover normal wear items (tires, brake pads, chains), crash damage, competitive racing, water submersion, or unauthorized aftermarket modifications.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-detail">
            <summary class="faq-summary">Do you offer monthly financing options?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p><strong>Yes! We offer flexible financing at checkout through Shop Pay Installments.</strong></p>
              <p>Eligible customers can split the total purchase amount into manageable bi-weekly or monthly payments. Select "Shop Pay" or "Affirm" at the payment step of checkout to view available terms, APR rates, and installment schedules with no impact on your credit score during initial eligibility pre-qualification.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

